{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794353397,"nonce":"9M2z24XYbIwvFJz7Rdwul0DNYZY=","message":"Every hand-written WGSL shader in blinc_gpu except canvas.wgsl and the custom pass templates is now russl: sdf_simple, text, image, path, the backdrop composite, liquid glass and simple glass, both mesh shaders, and the particle simulation and render pass (commits b271d5b8 through 0db59b89). Each port drew the same pixels as the WGSL it replaced over a scene that exercised every feature, with the temporary old-versus-new comparison mutation-checked for scene gaps, and the permanent tests are tier-versus-tier, CPU probes where the maths allows, pinned pixels, and goldens per machine. build.rs and the WGSL prelude are gone; canvas.wgsl carries its few helpers, since user shader code is spliced into it at run time and cannot be built ahead.\n\nrussl needed one more feature along the way: depth comparison sampling for the shadow map (russl commit 807e7b1). The russl commits not yet pushed are 61c94d6 (#if), cccaf0c (0.3.1) and 807e7b1.\n\nTwo defects in the core and image shaders turned up and are not fixed, to keep pixel parity: b1c5f7c (a Circle primitive's border only at four points) and ab55aa7 (an image border colour interpolated as a float).\n\nLeft: push russl main and tag v0.3.1, publish the russl crates, run the full CI list on a clean worktree of Blinc against them, then push Blinc.","files":null}]}